          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.46,
            0.115
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "7.5 Types of Triangles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.123,
            0.848,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": "In our study of triangles, we have encountered the following types of triangles; equilateral, isosceles, scalene and right-angled triangles."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.169,
            0.548,
            0.193
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Did you spot any other type of triangle?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.201,
            0.847,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "The classification of triangles as equilateral and isosceles was based on equality of sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.238,
            0.848,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": "Equilateral triangles have sides of equal length. Isosceles triangles have two sides of equal length. Scalene triangles have sides of three different lengths."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.332,
            0.344,
            0.458
          ],
